          <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
          <h2>ShiftWake Privacy Policy</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Last updated: October 15, 2026</p>
<h3>1. Scope</h3>
<p>This policy describes information handling by ShiftWake, an iPhone app provided by Wataru Ishibashi. Apple, RevenueCat and your calendar synchronization, messaging and email providers have their own policies.</p>
<h3>2. About the app</h3>
<p>ShiftWake schedules alarms using shift symbols or keywords in your iPhone Calendar. Optional user actions can create shift events or prepare an emergency message. Basic features are free; Apple and RevenueCat support paid-feature purchases and restoration.</p>
<h3>3. Information handled</h3>
<p>The app handles event titles, start times and calendar information needed for matching and scheduling; rules, alarm times, sounds and reservation state; local counters for setup dates, elapsed scheduled times, review requests and Pro-screen appearances; optional recipient phone numbers and message text; anonymous RevenueCat app user identifiers, purchase history and purchase/subscription status; and email addresses and message contents submitted for support. Elapsed reservation times do not confirm that someone woke up. The app has no account registration requiring a name, postal address or email; this does not mean no other information is processed.</p>
<h3>4. How information is obtained</h3>
<p>Calendar access uses the OS permission prompt. Rules and emergency details come from user input. Counters and reservation state are recorded locally as features run. Purchase status comes through Apple and RevenueCat. Support messages are received when you send email.</p>
<h3>5. Purposes</h3>
<p>Information supports shift matching, scheduling and updating alarms, creating requested events, enabling paid features, restoring purchases, managing subscriptions, choosing review-request timing, preparing optional messages and responding to support. RevenueCat also uses purchase information for validation and purchase analytics.</p>
<h3>6. Storage and transmission</h3>
<p>Rules, settings, reservation state, local counters and emergency settings are stored on the device. The current code does not implement sending Calendar contents or these counters to the developer&#x27;s server or RevenueCat. Alarm times and display labels, including rule/event names, are passed to the OS&#x27;s AlarmKit. Event creation writes to the device&#x27;s default calendar. Calendar synchronization follows your settings and the provider&#x27;s rules. Apple and RevenueCat process purchase-related information. Your emergency-message action passes the recipient and text to the messaging app; you review and send it. Email is transmitted when you submit it. Deleting the app may not delete Calendar events or third-party purchase records, and does not cancel subscriptions. Delete unwanted events in Calendar and manage subscriptions through Apple.</p>
<h3>7. Third parties</h3>
<p>The app has no feature that collects Calendar contents for the developer to distribute to third parties. However, Apple and RevenueCat process information needed for purchases, and your optional messages and email use external services. The app therefore does not claim that no information ever leaves the device. The current implementation does not use in-app ads or cross-app advertising tracking.</p>
<h3>8. External services</h3>
<p>Apple provides App Store payment and subscription management and OS calendar/alarm functions. RevenueCat provides validation, paid-feature access, restoration, subscription management and purchase analytics. Your chosen synchronization, messaging and email providers apply their own rules.
<a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple Privacy</a> / <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy-policy">RevenueCat Privacy</a></p>
<h3>9. Security</h3>
<p>OS permissions control Calendar access and can be changed in iPhone Settings. Settings are saved in OS-managed app storage. Purchase authentication and payment use Apple and RevenueCat&#x27;s systems. Device passcodes and OS updates are recommended. This policy does not promise an unverified encryption method, a custom authentication system or complete security.</p>
<h3>10. Minors</h3>
<p>The app has no birth-date entry for age verification. Minors should consult their guardians before purchases or sending messages and follow Apple and communication-provider requirements. Guardians can use device purchase controls. The app has no separate parental-consent verification system.</p>
<h3>11. Changes</h3>
<p>When features, services or information handling change, this policy will be reviewed and the page&#x27;s update date revised. Any required new OS permissions or store disclosures follow the relevant procedures.</p>
<h3>12. Contact</h3>
<p>For data-handling, purchase-record or technical questions, contact nyanyanyah@gmail.com. Do not send unnecessary personal Calendar or contact details, passwords or payment credentials. External providers&#x27; records and subscriptions may require their own deletion or management procedures.</p>
